custom-agents: dual-use security functionality

This package is a development assistant plugin and an explicit-command installer
for Claude Code, Codex and OpenCode. It includes security audit instructions,
local/private-target pentest helpers, security scanner orchestration, dependency
and secret scanning guidance, and examples used to verify defensive controls.
These capabilities can resemble offensive tooling and are declared as dual-use.

The intended legitimate use is authorized assessment and improvement of systems
owned by the operator or covered by explicit permission. Active testing helpers
are restricted to local/private targets. Scanner installation and external service
access follow the documented permission and configuration workflows. These
restrictions do not replace the operator's responsibility to obtain authorization.

Running the installer explicitly can write provider configuration and plugin
files and invoke provider CLIs. Installed hooks execute local helper processes.
The optional local dashboard can start and control native assistant sessions;
configured integrations can publish approved project knowledge or task updates to
selected services. These are runtime features, not npm install lifecycle scripts.
The package defines no preinstall, install or postinstall lifecycle script.

Security artifacts are kept separate from normal documentation publication.
Session journaling and knowledge publication are documented features with privacy
controls, bounded data handling and explicit integration configuration. This
disclosure describes intended functionality; it is not a claim that every defect
has been eliminated or a substitute for reviewing the source and configuration.

